\newlabel{fig:reexport_potential}{{10}{33}{Re-export Potential: Uzbekistan's Manufactured Goods Exports to Eurasian Markets (2023). Tile chart showing trade flow volumes (USD~billion) by destination and flow type; colour intensity $\propto $ trade value. Kazakhstan represents the largest near-term corridor. All flows remain below \$1~billion. Source: OEC/BACI bilateral trade data}{figure.caption.12}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {4.14}GVC Positioning: Backward and Forward Integration}{33}{subsection.4.14}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces GVC Positioning: Uzbekistan's Backward vs.\ Forward Integration, 2010--2023. The ideal trajectory is toward the upper-right quadrant; the \textit  {actual} trajectory moves rightward (increasing backward integration) but stagnates or declines vertically (forward integration), confirming captive governance. Backward proxy = intermediate goods share of imports from NE~Asia; Forward proxy = manufactured goods share of total exports. Colour: grey = pre-reform, orange = early reform (2017--2020), teal = post-COVID (2021--2023). Source: Author calculations from OEC/BACI and World Bank WDI data.}}{34}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gvc_positioning}{{11}{34}{GVC Positioning: Uzbekistan's Backward vs.\ Forward Integration, 2010--2023. The ideal trajectory is toward the upper-right quadrant; the \textit {actual} trajectory moves rightward (increasing backward integration) but stagnates or declines vertically (forward integration), confirming captive governance. Backward proxy = intermediate goods share of imports from NE~Asia; Forward proxy = manufactured goods share of total exports. Colour: grey = pre-reform, orange = early reform (2017--2020), teal = post-COVID (2021--2023). Source: Author calculations from OEC/BACI and World Bank WDI data}{figure.caption.13}{}}
